<title>USA: UAL says talks with attendants &quot;positive&quot;.</title>
<headline>UAL says talks with attendants &quot;positive&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines, the largest U.S. airline, said Tuesday that contract negotiations with its flight attendants remain &quot;positive&quot; and &quot;constructive,&quot; but no agreement has been reached.</p>
<p>The two sides have held contract talks over the past two weeks in Hawaii.</p>
<p>United, a unit of UAL Corp, recently finalized wage agreements with its pilots and machinists.  </p>
<p>The pact with the pilots and the machinists came after months of negotiations.</p>
</text>
